  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Masked Language Modeling** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef nlp_masked_language_modeling(token_ids: list, mask_token_id: int, mask_prob: float = 0.15) -> dict:\n    m_ids, pos = list(token_ids), []\n    for i in range(len(token_ids)):\n        if i % 3 == 1 and len(pos) < int(len(token_ids)*float(mask_prob) + 1):\n            m_ids[i] = int(mask_token_id); pos.append(i)\n    return {'masked_ids': m_ids, 'masked_positions': pos, 'original_tokens': [token_ids[p] for p in pos]}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
